---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';

const SECTIONS = [
  { id: 'what-is-ngfw', title: 'What is NGFW?' },
  { id: 'key-features', title: 'Key Features' },
  { id: 'how-it-works', title: 'How It Works' },
  { id: 'benefits', title: 'Benefits' },
  { id: 'vs-traditional', title: 'NGFW vs Traditional Firewall' },
];
---

<Layout title="Palo Alto NGFW Cheatsheet — Joven Talasan" description="Palo Alto Next-Generation Firewall core concepts: App-ID, User-ID, Content-ID, threat prevention, SSL decryption, and comparison with traditional firewalls.">
  <main>
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-12">
      <a href="/cheatsheet" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm mb-8" style="color: var(--accent)">
        ← back to cheatsheets
      </a>

      <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-2">
        <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest px-3 py-1 rounded-full" style="background: var(--accent); color: #1a1a1a">Security</span>
      </div>

      <h1 class="font-black uppercase tracking-tight mb-2" style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem); line-height: 0.95">
        Palo Alto <span style="color: var(--accent)">NGFW</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="text-sm mb-6" style="color: var(--text-muted)">Next-Generation Firewall — App-ID, User-ID, Content-ID, and advanced threat prevention.</p>

      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mb-8 text-xs font-mono" style="color: var(--text-faint)">
        <span>6 min read</span>
        <span>•</span>
        <span>5 sections</span>
      </div>

      <ul class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mb-10 text-xs font-mono">
        {SECTIONS.map(s => (
          <li>
            <a href={"#" + s.id} class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full border transition-colors" style="border-color: var(--border); color: var(--text-muted)">
              {s.title}
            </a>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>

      <div id="what-is-ngfw" class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-black uppercase tracking-wide mb-3" style="color: var(--text)">
          <a href="#what-is-ngfw" class="hover-underline">What is NGFW?</a>
        </h2>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--text-muted)">
          A Next-Generation Firewall (NGFW) is an advanced firewall that provides more than a
          traditional firewall. It goes beyond simple IP, port, and protocol filtering and provides
          deep visibility, threat prevention, and control over applications, users, and content.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-3 text-sm">
          <div class="p-3 rounded-xl border-2" style="background: var(--bg-card); border-color: var(--border)">
            <p class="font-bold mb-1" style="color: var(--text)">Next Generation Firewall</p>
            <ul class="space-y-1" style="color: var(--text-muted)">
              <li>Works on Application, User, Content, Threat</li>
              <li>Deep visibility of applications and users</li>
              <li>Identifies and controls applications (App-ID)</li>
              <li>Advanced threat prevention (IPS, Malware, URL filtering)</li>
              <li>SSL inspection to see inside encrypted traffic</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div id="key-features" class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-black uppercase tracking-wide mb-3" style="color: var(--text)">
          <a href="#key-features" class="hover-underline">Key Features of Palo Alto NGFW</a>
        </h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-3 text-sm">
          {[
            { t: 'App-ID', d: 'Identifies applications regardless of port or protocol.' },
            { t: 'User-ID', d: 'Identifies users and applies security policies based on identity.' },
            { t: 'Content-ID', d: 'Controls content (URLs, files, data) based on policies.' },
            { t: 'Threat Prevention', d: 'IPS, Anti-malware, Vulnerability protection, and more.' },
            { t: 'WildFire', d: 'Detects unknown threats using cloud-based sandboxing.' },
            { t: 'SSL Decryption', d: 'Decrypts SSL/TLS traffic to inspect for hidden threats.' },
            { t: 'Logging & Reporting', d: 'Provides detailed logs and reports for visibility and compliance.' },
          ].map(f => (
            <div class="p-3 rounded-xl border-2" style="background: var(--bg-card); border-color: var(--border)">
              <p class="font-bold mb-1" style="color: var(--accent)">{f.t}</p>
              <p style="color: var(--text-muted)">{f.d}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>

      <div id="how-it-works" class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-black uppercase tracking-wide mb-3" style="color: var(--text)">
          <a href="#how-it-works" class="hover-underline">How NGFW Works (Palo Alto)</a>
        </h2>
        <div class="text-sm p-4 rounded-xl border-2 font-mono leading-relaxed" style="background: var(--bg-card); border-color: var(--border); color: var(--text-muted)">
          <div style="color: var(--text)">Traffic → Palo Alto NGFW:</div>
          <ol class="space-y-1 mt-2 ml-4 list-decimal">
            <li>Identifies Application (App-ID)</li>
            <li>Identifies User (User-ID)</li>
            <li>Checks Content (Content-ID)</li>
            <li>Threat Prevention (IPS, AV, etc.)</li>
            <li>Decrypts SSL (if needed)</li>
            <li>Applies Security Policy</li>
            <li>Allows or Blocks Traffic</li>
          </ol>
          <div class="mt-3" style="color: var(--accent)">→ Secure Traffic</div>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm mt-4 leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--text-muted)">
          Palo Alto NGFW not only allows or blocks traffic, but also understands what the traffic is,
          who the user is, and whether it is safe or dangerous. That's why it is a Next Generation Firewall.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div id="benefits" class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-black uppercase tracking-wide mb-3" style="color: var(--text)">
          <a href="#benefits" class="hover-underline">Benefits</a>
        </h2>
        <ul class="space-y-1 text-sm" style="color: var(--text-muted)">
          <li>✓ Better visibility and control</li>
          <li>✓ Stops advanced threats</li>
          <li>✓ Improves security posture</li>
          <li>✓ Supports Zero Trust Security</li>
          <li>✓ Protects users, applications and data</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div id="vs-traditional" class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-black uppercase tracking-wide mb-3" style="color: var(--text)">
          <a href="#vs-traditional" class="hover-underline">NGFW vs Traditional Firewall</a>
        </h2>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto">
          <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead>
              <tr class="text-left font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wider">
                <th class="p-3 border font-bold" style="border-color: var(--border); color: var(--text)">Aspect</th>
                <th class="p-3 border font-bold" style="border-color: var(--border); color: var(--text)">Traditional Firewall</th>
                <th class="p-3 border font-bold" style="border-color: var(--border); color: var(--text)">NGFW (Palo Alto)</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="p-3 border font-medium" style="border-color: var(--border); color: var(--text)">Works on</td><td class="p-3 border" style="border-color: var(--border); color: var(--text-muted)">IP, Port, Protocol</td><td class="p-3 border" style="border-color: var(--border); color: var(--text-muted)">Application, User, Content, Threat</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="p-3 border font-medium" style="border-color: var(--border); color: var(--text)">Visibility</td><td class="p-3 border" style="border-color: var(--border); color: var(--text-muted)">Limited</td><td class="p-3 border" style="border-color: var(--border); color: var(--text-muted)">Deep application & user visibility</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="p-3 border font-medium" style="border-color: var(--border); color: var(--text)">Application Awareness</td><td class="p-3 border" style="border-color: var(--border); color: var(--text-muted)">No awareness of applications</td><td class="p-3 border" style="border-color: var(--border); color: var(--text-muted)">Full App-ID identification</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="p-3 border font-medium" style="border-color: var(--border); color: var(--text)">Security</td><td class="p-3 border" style="border-color: var(--border); color: var(--text-muted)">Basic (port/protocol blocking)</td><td class="p-3 border" style="border-color: var(--border); color: var(--text-muted)">Advanced (IPS, Anti-malware, WildFire)</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="p-3 border font-medium" style="border-color: var(--border); color: var(--text)">Encrypted Traffic</td><td class="p-3 border" style="border-color: var(--border); color: var(--text-muted)">Cannot see inside</td><td class="p-3 border" style="border-color: var(--border); color: var(--text-muted)">SSL decryption & inspection</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-16 p-4 rounded-xl border-2 text-center" style="background: var(--bg-card); border-color: var(--border)">
        <p class="text-xs font-mono" style="color: var(--text-faint)">
          Palo Alto NGFW not only allows or blocks traffic — it understands what the traffic is, who the user is, and whether it is safe or dangerous.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-8 text-center">
        <a href="/" class="inline-block px-6 py-3 font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-sm border-2 transition-all" style="background: var(--accent); color: #1a1a1a; border-color: #1a1a1a; box-shadow: 4px 4px 0 #1a1a1a; border-radius: 9999px">
          ← all cheatsheets
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    "itemListElement": [
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://talz.net" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Cheatsheets", "item": "https://talz.net/cheatsheet/" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "Palo Alto NGFW Cheatsheet", "item": "https://talz.net/cheatsheet/palo-alto/" }
    ]
  })} />
</Layout>
